# Design System Rules: Verse Studio

This project follows the **Verse Studio** design system. All UI changes must adhere to the following strict guidelines.

## 1. Design Tokens & Theming

**Source of Truth:** `tailwind.config.js` and `src/index.css`.

### Colors
Use Tailwind utility classes or CSS variables. **Do not hardcode hex values.**

| Token Name | Tailwind Class | CSS Variable | Hex Value | Usage |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Primary** | `text-primary` / `bg-primary` | `--primary` | `#5ab9ff` | Main actions, highlights, active states |
| **Background Dark** | `bg-background-dark` | `--bg-dark` | `#051324` | Main application background |
| **Surface Dark** | `bg-surface-dark` | `--surface-dark` | `#154270` | Secondary backgrounds, sidebars |
| **Sheet** | `bg-sheet` | `--sheet` | `#0e3359` | Modals, bottom sheets, panels (often with opacity) |
| **Card** | `bg-card` | `--card` | `#152e4d` | Content cards, data displays |
| **Text Primary** | `text-white` | `--text-primary` | `#ffffff` | Headings, body text |
| **Text Muted** | `text-white/60` | `--text-muted` | - | Secondary text, captions |

### Typography
Use the semantic font stacks defined in the config.

| Font Stack | Tailwind Class | Family | Usage |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Display/Sans** | `font-sans` | Inter | UI elements, headings, English text |
| **Arabic** | `font-arabic` | Noto Sans Arabic, Amiri | General Arabic text |
| **Uthmani** | `font-uthmani` | Amiri Quran | **Strictly for Quranic verses** |
| **Serif** | `font-serif` | Amiri | Quotes, poetic text |

### Effects & Glassmorphism
Use the custom utility classes for "glass" effects instead of manual opacity/blur.

*   **Standard Glass:** `.glass` (Backdrop blur 20px, border, shadow) - Used for panels, overlays.
*   **Card Glass:** `.glass-card` (Backdrop blur 12px) - Used for content cards.
*   **Input Glass:** `.glass-input` (Backdrop blur 8px) - Used for form fields.

## 2. Component Architecture

### Directory Structure
*   **Shared/Generic Atoms:** `src/components/` (e.g., `Button`, `Modal`, `Skeleton`).
*   **Feature-Specific:** `src/modules/<feature>/components/` (e.g., `src/modules/quran/components/VerseCard.tsx`).

### Component Pattern
*   **Functional Components:** Use `React.FC` or standard function declarations with typed props.
*   **Props Interface:** Always define a TypeScript interface for props, named `[ComponentName]Props`.
*   **Styling:** 
    1.  **Tailwind CSS** (Preferred for layout, spacing, typography).
    2.  **CSS Modules** (`[Name].module.css`) for complex animations or highly specific selectors that Tailwind handles poorly.

```tsx
// Example Component Pattern
import { motion } from 'framer-motion';
import { IconBook } from '@/components/Icons';

interface VerseCardProps {
  verseKey: string;
  text: string;
}

export const VerseCard = ({ verseKey, text }: VerseCardProps) => {
  return (
    <div className="glass-card p-4 rounded-xl hover:border-primary/50 transition-colors">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <IconBook className="w-5 h-5 text-primary" />
        <span className="font-sans text-sm text-white/60">{verseKey}</span>
      </div>
      <p className="font-uthmani text-2xl text-right leading-loose">{text}</p>
    </div>
  );
};
```

## 3. Icon System

**Primary Source:** `lucide-react`
**Secondary Source:** `src/components/Icons.tsx` (Custom branding/specific icons)

*   **Usage Rule:** Check `src/components/Icons.tsx` first. If the icon exists there (e.g., `IconQuran`, `IconMosque`), use it to maintain branding consistency. If not, use `lucide-react`.
*   **Styling:** Icons usually accept a `className` prop. Size them using Tailwind (e.g., `w-5 h-5`).

## 4. Asset Management

*   **Static Assets:** Place in `public/`. Reference as strings: `"/images/logo.png"`.
*   **Imported Assets:** Place in `src/assets/`. Import directly: `import logo from '@/assets/branding/logo.png'`.
*   **Video:** Use the `public/videos/` directory.

## 5. Animation (Framer Motion)

*   Use `framer-motion` for complex interactions (enter/exit, layout changes).
*   Use standard Tailwind `animate-*` classes (defined in config) for simple loops (e.g., `animate-pulse-slow`, `animate-float`).

## 6. Development Workflow (MCP Integration)

When generating code from Figma or specs:
1.  **Identify the Module:** Determine if the component belongs to a specific module (e.g., `quran`, `auth`) or is shared.
2.  **Map Tokens:** Translate Figma hex codes to the nearest Verse Studio token (e.g., `#5ab9ff` -> `text-primary`).
3.  **Use Glass Utilities:** Detect translucent backgrounds in design and apply `.glass` or `.glass-card` classes instead of raw CSS opacity.
4.  **Check Typography:** If text is Arabic, strictly apply `font-arabic` or `font-uthmani` based on context.
